{"learnerLanguage":"en","spokenSeconds":210,"turns":[{"speaker":"character","text":"Good morning. My name is Emma. Could you tell me your full name, please?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Good morning. My name is Camille Durand."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Do you work or are you a student?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I work as a nurse in a hospital in Lyon. I am doing this job since two years, and honestly the first months were overwhelming, but now I feel more confident with the patients."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Describe a skill you learned recently. Say what the skill is, how you learned it, how difficult it was, and explain why you wanted to learn it."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I recently learned to cook Indian food, because my flatmate is from Mumbai and she cooks amazing dishes. At the beginning it was a steep learning curve, there are so many spices and I didn't know which one to use. She showed me step by step, and then I watched videos in the evening. It was more easy than I thought once I understood the basic mix of spices. I wanted to learn it because I think sharing food is a way to understand another culture, and also, to be honest, I was tired of eating pasta every day."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Do you think people should learn practical skills at school?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Yes, I am agree with that. On the other hand, schools already have a lot of subjects, so it depends of how they organize the time. But skills like cooking or managing money are useful for everybody, that's why I think they deserve a place in the program."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Is it easier to learn a skill from a person or from the internet?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"It depends of the skill. For something physical, like cooking or sport, a person can correct you directly. With the internet you have more choice, but nobody tells you when you do a mistake."}],"criteria":[{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"fluencyCoherence","levelBand":null,"name":"Fluency and Coherence","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"lexicalResource","levelBand":null,"name":"Lexical Resource","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"grammar","levelBand":null,"name":"Grammatical Range and Accuracy","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"pronunciation","levelBand":null,"name":"Pronunciation","scope":"task","sound":true,"voiceOnly":true}],"task":{"brief":"The test's three parts in a shorter call","minutes":{"max":5,"min":5},"name":"Speaking mock","role":"examiner"},"title":"IELTS Speaking","exam":"ielts"}